{
    "map": {
        "anchor_points.descr": "The path and name of the feature class that contains anchor points. Anchor points overlay vertices on the input features and indicate that they should not be moved or deleted in the simplify process.",
        "anchor_points.title": "Anchor Points",
        "circular_arcs.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether circular arcs will be created.</p><ul><li>Checked—Circular arcs will be created. This is the default.</li><li>Unchecked—Circular arcs will not be created.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "circular_arcs.title": "Create circular arcs",
        "closed_ends.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether the endpoints of a closed line will be preserved. A closed line is a line that has coincident end points (loop).</p><ul><li>Checked—The endpoints of closed lines will be preserved. This is the default.</li><li>Unchecked—The endpoints of closed lines will not be preserved; they can be moved or deleted.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "closed_ends.title": "Preserve endpoints for closed line",
        "description": "Simplifies polygon and line features by replacing consecutive line segments  or edges with  fewer line segments or edges. Lines segments and polygon edges are simplified based on a specified maximum allowable offset.  Additionally, circular arcs can be created from consecutive  line segments or polygon edges.",
        "fitting_type.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies how the output feature edges and circular arcs will be fitted to the input feature shapes.</p><p>If <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Fit to segments</span> is specified, the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Maximum Arc Angle Step</span> and <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Minimum Number Of Vertices</span> parameters are not available.</p><ul><li><span title=\"FIT_TO_VERTICES\">Fit to vertices</span>—The offset gap between the output feature edges and the input feature vertices will be minimized. Output feature edges and curves will be fitted approximately to the input feature vertex positions. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"FIT_TO_SEGMENTS\">Fit to segments</span>—The offset gap between the output feature edges and input feature edges will be minimized. Output edges and curves will be fitted approximately to the positions of the input feature shapes.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "fitting_type.domain.FIT_TO_SEGMENTS": "Fit to segments",
        "fitting_type.domain.FIT_TO_VERTICES": "Fit to vertices",
        "fitting_type.title": "Fitting Type",
        "in_features.descr": "The features to be simplified. Features can be lines or polygons. If using multiple inputs, the features must have the same spatial reference.",
        "in_features.title": "Input Features",
        "max_arc_angle_step.descr": "<xdoc><p>The maximum arc angle step (decimal degrees) that will be used to construct circular arcs. The arc angle defines how wide the visual field can be, for each step, when locating vertices to construct circular curves. The arc angle is the central angle of the candidate curve (the curve that is being constructed). If vertices are found within each maximum arc angle step, a circular arc is constructed. For example, if vertices and edges are sparse, use a large arc angle step. The valid value range is from 2 through 95 decimal degrees. The default is 20 decimal degrees. This parameter is not available if the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Fit to segments</span> option is specified for the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Fitting Type</span> parameter.</p></xdoc>",
        "max_arc_angle_step.title": "Maximum Arc Angle Step (decimal degrees)",
        "max_offset.descr": "<xdoc><p>The maximum distance the output feature edges can deviate from the input feature shapes. When the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Fit to vertices</span> option is specified for the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Fitting Type</span> parameter, the distance is measured between the input vertices and the output feature edges. When the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Fit to segments</span> option is specified, the distance is measured between the input feature edges and the output feature edges.</p></xdoc>",
        "max_offset.title": "Maximum Allowable Offset",
        "max_radius.descr": "<xdoc><p>The largest allowable radius for output circular arcs. The value must be greater than the value provided for <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Minimum Radius</span>. If no value is provided, the radius of the output circular arcs will not checked (default).</p></xdoc>",
        "max_radius.title": "Maximum Radius",
        "min_arc_angle.descr": "The minimum arc angle (decimal degrees) that will be used to construct circular arcs. The minimum arc angle is the smallest allowable central angle in the output circular arcs. If the central angle of any output circular arc is less than this value, it will not be created. The valid value range is from 2 through 360 decimal degrees. The default is 2 decimal degrees.",
        "min_arc_angle.title": "Minimum Arc Angle (decimal degrees)",
        "min_radius.descr": "<xdoc><p>The smallest allowable radius for output circular arcs. The value must be greater than 0 and smaller than the value provided for <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Maximum Radius</span>. If no value is provided, the radius of the output circular arcs will not be checked (default).</p></xdoc>",
        "min_radius.title": "Minimum Radius",
        "min_vertex_count.descr": "<xdoc><p>The minimum number of vertices required for a circular arc to be created. The value must be greater than 3. The default is 4. This parameter is not available if the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Fit to segments</span> option is specified for the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Fitting Type</span> parameter.</p></xdoc>",
        "min_vertex_count.title": "Minimum Number Of Vertices",
        "out_feature_class.title": "Output Features",
        "out_feature_layers.title": "Output Layer Names",
        "summary": "Simplifies polygon and line features by replacing consecutive line segments or edges with fewer line segments or edges. Lines segments and polygon edges are simplified based on a specified maximum allowable offset. Additionally, circular arcs can be created from consecutive line segments or polygon edges.",
        "title": "Simplify By Straight Lines And Circular Arcs"
    }
}
